        "orario": "16:48",
        "timestamp": 1780498092,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. A year before the French election, De Gaulle remains politically fashionable France Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 16:48 Modified: 03/06/2026 - 16:48 ‘De Gaulle: Resistance’, is released in cinemas in France on June 3, the first part of a two-parter on Charles de Gaulle, the French general and statesman who led the Free French Forces against Nazi Germany and Vichy France. The much anticipated films took director Antonin Baudry and his team six years to make, with a budget of nearly 80 million euros. But even beyond the silver screen, with a year to go until the presidential elections, De Gaulle has perhaps never been so politically fashionable. Under Paris's Notre Dame, archaeologists are unearthing 2,000 years of history 03/06/2026 France 1994 Tutsi Genocide: 'French government has never fully come to terms with its involvement' 02/06/2026 Africa Russian oil tanker intercepted by France and allies in Atlantic 01/06/2026 RUSSIA France mourns intellectual 'grandfather', sociologist and philosopher Edgar Morin 30/05/2026 France \"Choose France\" summit to kick off as factory closures multiply 30/05/2026 France A year ahead of the French presidential election, where do candidates stand? 26/05/2026 France 'Heat dome': Heatwave conditions hit France and parts of Europe 26/05/2026 France Paris's Notre Dame cathedral in the midst of a battle over its stained glass 26/05/2026 France Tennis legend Gael Monfils says goodbye to French Open ahead of retirement 26/05/2026 France"
